<Shell title="Commenting guidelines" narrow><article class="prose"><h1>Commenting guidelines</h1><p>Comments are for responses to the chapter you have read. Agreement, disagreement, and uncertainty are welcome.</p><ul><li>Discuss the chapter’s reasoning and your reading experience.</li><li>Treat other readers respectfully. Avoid personal attacks, harassment, or hateful language.</li><li>Do not post spam, advertisements, or someone else’s private information.</li><li>Use plain text, up to 2,000 characters, in any language.</li></ul><p>You do not need to submit a rating to comment. A name or nickname is optional and is not verified. Comments appear publicly after submission.</p><p>You can edit or delete your own comments from the browser that posted them. Use Report to bring a comment to the administrator’s attention. A report does not automatically hide a comment.</p><p><a href="/">Return to chapters</a></p></article></Shell>
